The generated server bundles @zodiacs/engine 0.1.1-rc.16 and astronomy-engine
2.1.19. Engine code is MIT; its Delta-T data includes CC BY 4.0 values from
Stephenson, Morrison and Hohenkerk (2016). Preserve ENGINE-NOTICE, ENGINE-LICENSE
and ENGINE-LICENSING, copied unchanged from the installed published engine.
astronomy-engine's full MIT notice remains in the generated JavaScript.

The bundled local civil-time resolver carries the site's pinned IANA Time
Zone Database 2025c histories before 1970 and zone-name/local-mean-time tables.
IANA timezone data is public domain: https://www.iana.org/time-zones.
From 1970, resolution uses the Node host's Intl/ICU timezone data.

The MCP SDK 2.0.0 and Zod 4.6.5 stay external and retain the license files in
their installed packages. Plugin dependencies also install the published
engine, with its own notices, for the runnable examples.
